{"id": "E0118", "idea": {"id": "I243", "category": "strategy", "priority": 1, "source": "meta", "status": "trying:lane3", "source_experiments": ["E0046", "E0101"], "evaluation": {"elo0": 0, "elo1": 15, "max_pairs": 2400, "fresh": true}, "title": "At the unit cap, long dragons go where there is room: target choice counts how crowded the ground around a target is", "hypothesis": "Big-picture change to where long dragons go once the swarm fills the map. At the 64 cap a doomed dragon can't split out, and since E0101 (split gates off) we reach the cap sooner and hold it longer (online 261292: 64 alive from r100 to r450). Online 6736+6778 (90 games): before r415 our dragons >= 8 long died trapped (not head-on) 2.7 times a game at the cap, 43.7 segments a game, against 0.34 (5.6 segments) below it; the opponents in the same games lost 1.37 (17.8 segments) at their cap. E0046's post-mortem found teammate bodies around the dead head in 86-96% of these deaths (I083): our own swarm walls long dragons in. I083 fixes the room check that misjudges a teammate's freeing tail; this changes the plan that walks them into crowds: while World::unitCount is at the unit limit, a dragon at least P.roomMinLength (start 8) long scores each pearl or explore target candidate with a crowding cost P.crowdWeight (start 1 step) per teammate body tile (seen, or in the belief map's recent views) within Chebyshev 3 of the target, so it prefers pearls and frontier in open ground; below the cap or for shorter dragons nothing changes. The coder may choose another crowding measure the bot already has (e.g. the target's flood-fill room with bodies standing) and says why. Boundaries: a pearl within 2 steps is still taken; on small walled maps where every target is crowded the order is today's. Scenarios: at the cap, a 12-long dragon between a pearl 5 steps away inside a knot of teammate bodies and one 7 steps away in open ground takes the open one; the same below the cap, or a 4-long dragon, takes the nearer. Report per game (logging copy vs champion, swarm and breeder on near_big_empty, near_schooltime and mix maps): long trapped deaths at the cap before r415 and their segments, our longest at r400 and r499.", "history": ["E0106 kept I083, which this idea cites: raised to priority 1; check whether what it was waiting on is now there"]}, "lane": 3, "base": "2c79f81d0d90038543c82dff930ce243cc4b16e8", "candidate": "7e4b60b1f9a49decf45b4e4ba0ae1831a14d6b50", "changed_files": ["bot/params.hpp", "bot/state.hpp", "bot/targets.hpp", "tests/bot/test_state.cpp", "tests/bot/test_targets.cpp"], "session": {"parent": "bc-main-fresh", "name": "bc-E0118-89613581", "session_id": "89613581-b225-4bdd-b097-8facbe6928f7", "status": "finished"}, "cpu": {"ok": true, "line": "CPU PASS p50 3.6M p99 5.7M max 7.2M timeouts 0 crashes 0 no-action-deaths 0 (3 games, 104560 turns)"}, "bot_tests": {"ok": true, "line": "bot tests: 15 scenario binaries + 1 protocol suite; 0 failed"}, "sprt": {"decision": "inconclusive", "error": null, "llr": 0.4132561354188911, "lower": -2.9444389791664403, "upper": 2.9444389791664403, "elo0": 0.0, "elo1": 15.0, "alpha": 0.05, "beta": 0.05, "pairs": 2400, "pentanomial": [40, 0, 87, 0, 2124, 0, 92, 0, 57], "score": 0.504062493229178, "elo": 2.8229715484856603, "elo_lo": -0.5533132959061386, "elo_hi": 6.199789652576125, "nelo": 8.218022471494995, "rotation": ["champion", "swarm", "rammer", "breeder"], "per_opponent": {"champion": {"trials": 600, "score": 0.5066666666666667}, "swarm": {"trials": 600, "score": 0.50625}, "rammer": {"trials": 600, "score": 0.5004166666666666}, "breeder": {"trials": 600, "score": 0.5029166666666667}}, "cand": "/Users/me/.bc-loop/runs/E0118/cand", "base": "/Users/me/.bc-loop/champion/bot", "baselines_reused": 1412, "predict": {"checks": 100, "identical": 0, "predicted": 0, "audited": 0, "audit_mismatches": 0, "check_cpu": 7.9886219579999995, "off": "only 0 of the first 100 checks were identical"}, "per_style": {"mix": {"trials": 1333, "sco