{"id": "E0125", "idea": {"id": "I196", "category": "map", "priority": 1, "title": "Read the map's guaranteed symmetry: identify the mirror from paired sightings, then write each seen tile's kelp, portals and spawn countdown into its mirror", "hypothesis": "Rules and API inventory (review 1790355075914626000). docs/unsw/map-info.md guarantees every map is symmetric by a vertical mirror, a horizontal mirror or a 180-degree rotation ('that one's up to you'); map-files.md and pearls.md say mirrored tiles share one pearl countdown and fire together; kelp-and-portals.md says portals map onto portals under the symmetry. The champion reads none of it: World (state.hpp) assumes every unseen edge open, learns a tile's countdown only by seeing it, and its fast-tile evidence comes from resets it watched itself. I011 (E0014 ended at a session limit before any code) proposed detecting it. Change, a World capability with its consumers unchanged, behind P.useSymmetry: keep the three candidate mirrors; drop a candidate once a tile and its candidate mirror, both known (our vision, or a teammate's view in the belief map), disagree on an edge kind (open, kelp, portal) or a countdown (spawnRound at the same round, or -1 against a spawning tile); once one candidate remains, every tile we see also writes its mirror's edges, spawnKind, spawnRound and reset evidence into memory (identical by the rules), so paths, pearl and spawn targets, explore staleness of spawn tiles, fast-tile farms and the unknown-portal rules see the mirror half. Measure first with a logging copy on the 9 ladder, 2 sprint and about 10 fresh eval maps (mapgen keeps maps symmetric): the round at which one candidate remains (alone and with belief views), the share of the map's edges known at r50 and r100 with and without, and how often the chosen pearl or explore target, or its path length, changes. Expected: dragons crossing the middle route around kelp they have not seen and aim at spawn tiles that fire on arrival, and fast tiles watched on one side count on both. Boundary: until one candidate remains nothing changes; a tile on the axis mirrors onto itself; a wrong candidate kept by mistake is caught by the next disagreement and all mirrored writes are dropped; a split child starts with no symmetry until it sees a pair or hears a view. Scenarios: a 32x16 x-mirror map where seeing kelp at (3,5) and open ground at its y-mirror drops the y candidate; after identification a pearl behind mirrored kelp gets its true path length.", "status": "trying:lane3", "source": "meta", "evaluation": {"elo0": 0, "elo1": 15, "max_pairs": 2400, "fresh": true}, "history": ["2026-09-26 15:25 orchestrator (never-tested triage): priority 3 -> 2. Holds I011 (map symmetry), never played (E0014 left no code). We trail the dev benchmark on map seen by r100 (67% vs 80%); exploration gave E0102 +41.6.", "2026-09-26 16:22 orchestrator: priority 3 -> 2 again; the 15:4x review apply had reverted the 15:21/15:25 change (fixed in meta.apply_review)"]}, "lane": 3, "base": "7e4b60b1f9a49decf45b4e4ba0ae1831a14d6b50", "candidate": "d52bfb4cac1a2706f791636d1bc8970b0718d59e", "changed_files": ["bot/main.cpp", "bot/params.hpp", "bot/state.hpp", "bot/symmetry.hpp", "bot/targets.hpp", "tests/bot/test_symmetry.cpp"], "session": {"parent": "bc-main-fresh", "name": "bc-E0125-3fc9e284", "session_id": "3fc9e284-813c-478c-94d1-bb8254c72882", "status": "finished"}, "cpu": {"ok": true, "line": "CPU PASS p50 4.2M p99 5.8M max 8.1M timeouts 0 crashes 0 no-action-deaths 0 (11 games, 195999 turns)"}, "bot_tests": {"ok": true, "line": "bot tests: 16 scenario binaries + 1 protocol suite; 0 failed"}, "sprt": {"decision": "H1", "error": null, "llr": 3.0621211898231047, "lower": -2.9444389791664403, "upper": 2.9444389791664403, "elo0": 0.0, "elo1": 15.0, "alpha": 0.05, "beta": 0.05, "pairs": 504, "pentanomial": [16, 0, 50, 1, 336, 1, 66, 1, 33], "score": 0.5255448401888092, "elo": 17.765840991925394, "elo_lo": 5.866334447374352, "elo_hi": 2